' TLocale.SetUpKeyStrings
' VA 0x004C5966   6214 bytes   vtable slot 0x3c   sig ()i
' byte-identical vs NSS5.exe (6214/6214, original length from Ghidra's inventory)
' mode=reloc (570 bytes of absolute addresses masked: the 114 string-constant
'   pointers, the module-global slot 0xC5A324 and the TLocale class-table slot
'   0xC5A428 through which GetLocaleText is dispatched)
' ASSUMPTIONS:
'   * module Global at 0x00C5A324 declared String[] (globals_named.tsv calls it
'     g_options_arr01 / Object[]; String[] is what the assignments require and it
'     produces identical code). Element i lives at ptr+0x18+4*i, i.e. a 1-D BBArray,
'     cross-checked against TOptions.GetButtonLabel which reads ptr+i*4+0x18.
'   * indices are written as raw integers; they are exactly BRL.Keycodes' KEY_*
'     values, so the original almost certainly used the constant names -- constants
'     fold, so codegen is unaffected either way.
'   * string literal CONTENT does not affect code bytes (only the masked pointer);
'     each literal here was read out of NSS5.exe's data at the pushed address.
'   * duplicate indices (107, 109) and the out-of-order 13-before-12 pair are in the
'     original's emission order and are reproduced verbatim.

